%I A401329 #12 Oct 28 2026 17:41:29
%S A401329 2,3286,4210,5182,54214,127330
%N A401329 Least elements of periodic cycles of the map T(n) = n + D(n) - D(n+1), where D(n) is the largest positive proper divisor of n.
%C A401329 a(7), if it exists, exceeds 10^9.
%H A401329 Adrien Washington, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23357210">The Six-Trap Conjecture, Version 1.0</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A401329 Adrien Washington, <a href="https://github.com/adrienlwashington/six-trap-conjecture">Six-Trap Conjecture GitHub repository</a>.
%e A401329 For example, 3286 is a term because 3286 -> 4756 -> 7063 -> 4540 -> 6571 -> 3286, and 3286 is the least element of this period-5 cycle.
%Y A401329 Cf. A032742 (largest proper divisor function), A020639 (least prime factor).
%K A401329 nonn,more,new
%O A401329 1,1
%A A401329 _Adrien Washington_, Oct 21 2026
